      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:1:11:2",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ الْعَسْكَرِيَّ ( عليه السلام ) بِالْمَدِينَةِ عَنْ رَجُلٍ أَوْصَى بِمَالٍ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ فَقَالَ سَبِيلُ اللَّهِ شِيعَتُنَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Ja’far Al Razaaz, from Muhammad Bin Isa and Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Muhammad Bin Ahmad, from Muhammad Bin Isa Bin Ubeyd, from Al Hassan Bin Rashid who said, ",
          "‘I asked (Imam) Al-Askary<sup>asws</sup> at Al-Medina about a man who had bequeathed wealth to be in the Way of Allah<sup>azwj</sup>. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The Way of Allah<sup>azwj</sup>, is (a reference to) our<sup>asws</sup> Shias’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Muhammad ibn Ja‘far al-Raziy has narrated from Muhammad ibn ‘Isa and Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Isa ibn ‘Ubayd from al-Hassan ibn Rashid who has narrated the following: “I once asked al-‘Askariy, Alayhi al-Salam, in al-Madinah about the case of a man who has made a will to spend in the way of Allah. He (the Imam) said, ‘In the way of Allah is our Shi ’ah (followers).”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
